## SAGA PATTERN KI LIMITATIONS :
-----------------------------------

1:  TEMPORARY DATA INCONSISTENCY 
----------------------------------
   Saga Pattern mein har Service apni Local Transaction independently commit karti hai. 
   Isliye Saga execution ke beech kuch time ke liye participating Services ke Databases 
   ka data temporarily inconsistent state mein ho sakta hai.

   ## EXAMPLE:
   ------------

   Order Service
    → Start Local Transaction on Order DB
    → Create Order
    → COMMIT

   Inventory Service
    → Start Local Transaction on Inventory DB
    → Reserve Inventory
    → COMMIT

   Payment Service
    → Start Local Transaction on Payment DB
    → Process Payment...


   Is temporary state mein Order aur Inventory ke databases successfully update
   ho chuke hain, lekin Payment abhi complete nahi hui hai.

   Agar saare Local database Transactions successfully complete ho jaati hain, to eventually
   sabhi participating  Servies ke Databases consistent state mein aa jaate hain.

   Aur agar kisi bhi Local database transaction mein failure ho jaata hai, to previously successfully 
   completed Local database transactions ke effects ko reverse karne ke liye Compensating Transactions
   execute ki jaati hain. Compensating Transactions complete hone ke baad, sabhi participating Databases
   phir se eventually consistent state mein aa jaate hain.

   Isliye Saga Pattern Immediate Consistency provide nahi karta, balki system ko eventually Consistent State mein laata hai.


2:  COMPENSATING TRANSACTIONS KA OVERHEAD
-------------------------------------------

    Saga Pattern mein agar kisi later Local Transaction mein failure ho jaata hai, to pehle successfully
    completed Local Transactions ke business effects ko logically reverse karne ke liye respective Databases 
    par Compensating Transactions execute karni padti hain.

    Kyuki har participating Service apni respective Database ke andar apni Local Database Transaction ko independently
    execute aur commit karti hai, isliye ek Service ki Local Transaction fail hone ki wajah se doosri Services ki previously
    committed Local Database Transactions automatically rollback nahi hoti hain.

    Isliye failure ki situation mein previously successful local Transaction ke business effects ko explicitly 
    reverse karne ke liye Compensating transactions ko separately implement aur execute karna padta hai.

    Ye additional application logic, compensation handling aur implementation complexity introduce karta hai.



3: FAILURE HANDLING AND RETRY COMPLEXITY
------------------------------------------

  Distributed Environment mein Network Failure ya Timeout ki wajah 
  se kisi write operation ka actual result uncertain ho sakta hai.

  ### EXAMPLE:
  -------------

  Maan lo ek E-commerce Application mein Order Service, Inventory Service aur Payment Service Saga 
  Orchestration Pattern ke through ek Order process kar rahi hain.

  Saga Orchestrator Payment Service ko Payment process karne ke liye instruct karta hai.

  Payment Service Payment successfully process karke Payment Database mein persist kar deti hai, 
  lekin uska response Saga Orchestrator tak pahunchne se pehle Network Timeout ho jaata hai.

  Ab Saga Orchestrator ko clear nahi hoga ki Payment Successfully process hui thi, ya Actually fail hui thi.

  Agar Saga Orchestrator Payment Process karne wali Write Operation ko blindly retry kare aur Payment pehle 
  hi successfully process ho chuki ho, to Customer ko duplicate charge kiya ja sakta hai.

  Isliye Saga ke Write Operations ko generally Idempotent design karna important hota hai. 
  Yaani same Write Operation ko multiple times retry karne ke baad bhi final business result incorrect nahi hona chahiye.

  ### EXAMPLE:
  ------------ 
  Agar paymentId = P123 ke liye Payment pehle hi successfully process ho chuki hai,
  to same paymentId = P123 ke saath retry request aane par Payment Service ko Customer 
  ko dobara charge nahi karna chahiye.

  Isliye Saga Pattern mein Network Failures, Timeouts aur Retries ko correctly
  handle karne ke liye additional logic implement karna padta hai, jisse overall 
  implementation complexity increase ho sakti hai.


4: COMPENSATING TRANSACTION KHUD BHI FAIL HO SAKTI HAI
---------------------------------------------------------

  Saga Pattern mein agar kisi Local Transaction mein failure ho jaata hai, to previously successfully
  completed Local Transactions ke business effects ko reverse karne ke liye Compensating Transactions 
  execute ki jaati hain.
  
  Lekin Compensating Transaction khud bhi fail ho sakti hai.

  ## EXMAPLE:
  ------------
   Payment Process → FAIL   
   ↓
   Restore Inventory → FAIL

  Aisi situation mein Compensating Transaction ke failure aur retries ko properly handle karna padta hai.

  Saath hi, jis Service mein Compensating Transaction execute hoti hai, us Service ko Compensation Write Operation
  ko generally Idempotent design karna hota hai, taaki same Compensation Write Operation multiple times retry hone par 
  bhi uska business effect sirf ek baar apply ho.
 
  Ye additional failure-handling, retry aur idempotency logic implementation complexity introduce karte hain.
 



